Error
 - In Go, an error is just an interface with a method which returns a string.
 - errors.New("user not found"), for a fixed message
 - fmt.Errorf("user %d not found", id), for a formatting an error message
 - Do not ignore errors

Error wrapping:
 - fmt.Errorf("failed to get user: %w", err)
 - %v → format error → string
 - %w → wrap error → new error preserving original error, creates a wrapped error chain
 - %w wraps an error while preserving the error chain, allowing errors.Is and errors.As to inspect the underlying errors. 
   %v only formats the error into the message and does not preserve the wrapping relationship.
